      "writtenOn": "2024-10-02T20:54:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This relies on the fact that the java library has \"system_ext_specific: true\". A Mainline module owner can easily miss that because the jar isn\u0027t actually installed to system_ext. How do you enforce that?\n\nEven if the java library has \"system_ext_specific: true\", `PathForModuleInstall` returns a fake path, so this code relies on the fake path. I think this is a bit awkward.\n\nIs there a better approach (e.g., getting the partition of the apex)?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 496,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 496,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "fbdb3c73b290db776349ff8e78ad52cc21badb8c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7305377a_ae153316",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 496,
      "author": {
        "id": 1878380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-02T21:43:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point, I think we need an enforcement that these properties do not diverge. I have a WIP CL (https://r.android.com/3289228, next CL in this stack) to enforce that.\n\nGetting this information from the partition of the apex would be ideal, but I think that would require a top down mutator, which is not very friendly with partial analysis (b/367784740). Alternatively, maybe we can move these build rules from the context of the the apex system server jar to the context of the top-level apex?\n\nUsing the `system_ext_specific` property of the javalib and creating an enforcement that it matches the `system_ext_specific` property of the top-level apex seemed like the simpler solution.",
      "parentUuid": "283366b7_f730363b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 496,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 496,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "fbdb3c73b290db776349ff8e78ad52cc21badb8c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d4186c0_dc807d50",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 496,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T10:00:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. We already have a mutator that sets `ApexInfoProvider`. Is it possible to propagate `system_ext_specific` from there?",
      "parentUuid": "7305377a_ae153316",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 496,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 496,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "fbdb3c73b290db776349ff8e78ad52cc21badb8c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "87627bba_643b992a",
        "filename": "java/dexpreopt.go",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 496,
      "author": {
        "id": 1878380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T17:57:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think `ApexInfoProvider` relies on `AllApexInfoProvider`, which is currently set using the topDown `apexInfo` mutator. top down mutators are currently in a state of flux and are being migrated to transition mutators.\n\nWhen `apexInfo` mutator becomes a transition mutator, I think we can propagate this information using a configuration transition. But configuration transitions have some complexity, and propagating the information up from the java library and doing the check on the top-level apex seems like the simpler solution.\n\nIt does require more effort from module authors to set `system_ext_specific` to true on the java library, (and soong will raise an error if they dont), but I think it is worth the additional effort.",
      "parentUuid": "5d4186c0_dc807d50",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 496,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 496,
        "endChar": 58
      },
      "revId": "fbdb3c73b290db776349ff8e78ad52cc21badb8c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
